Description: slurmctld: retain external --no-kill jobs when their node goes DOWN
 A running external job (EXTERNAL_JOB, as slurm-bridge submits) with
 kill_on_node_fail=0 keeps its whole allocation (nodes, CPUs, memory, GRES)
 when its node goes DOWN, instead of failing with NODE_FAIL. Covers explicit
 state=down, SlurmdTimeout and "unexpectedly rebooted"; FUTURE and forced
 power-down still kill. The DOWN node takes no new work, returns ALLOCATED
 (resume / ReturnToService), refuses deletion while it holds the job (Slinky
 1.1.0's preStop runs "state=down && scontrol delete"), and keeps the job
 across a slurmctld restart. libslurm keeps reporting such a node DOWN instead
 of inferring MIXED. Hetjobs and jobs that did not opt in are unchanged.
 .
 Touches slurmctld and libslurm (src/api), so it matters for the slurmctld,
 slurmrestd, login and slurmd images. Source: meshy/retain-external-on-node-down
 on a SchedMD/slurm checkout at tag slurm-25-11-8-1. Regenerate on every
 SLURM_VERSION bump.
Author: Charlie Getzen <charliegetzen@meshy.ai>
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-05
